.TH MADVISE 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
madvise \- advise the kernel about a mapping
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/mman.h>
.B int madvise(void* address, size_t byte_count, int advice);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Applies a Linux MADV_* operation to a page\-aligned range. In particular,
MADV_DONTNEED and MADV_FREE affect the contents or reclamation of memory;
consult madvise(2) before using them.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero, or \-1 with errno set. Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR madvise (2)
